    "done_when": "tests in tests/test_follow_rearm_continues.py assert, through the follower generator, that a re-arm with nothing new draws exactly one row per live run, that a re-arm after a quiet baseline arming draws the fleet, that a replaced stream draws each live run once with the moved run carrying its recorded transition time, that each row renders the local clock of its run's recorded state time rather than the arming time, that rows arrive in ascending recorded-time order, and that no run appears twice in one arming even when it also moved in the gap. The first-arming Monitor case in tests/test_attach_shows_each_live_run.py asserts recorded times too. The attach paragraph in skills/reckon-build/references/orchestrator-harness/claude-code.md states this contract. The declared mutation, stamping replayed rows with the arming time, is observed to fail with its log recorded. The follow, ticker, watch and row-policy test files show zero added failures by id against the dispatch base, with base and head logs under the run directory, each headed with its revision and tree",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "every arming of crew follow, a re-arm included, draws one row per live run stamped with the recorded time that run entered its current state, in ascending time order, so a re-arm is never blank nor a burst of rows stamped with the attach time",
